/-!
# A cartesian module on a site of affine schemes with flat coverings is a sheaf

Let `C` be a category with pullbacks equipped with a functor `L : C ⥤ Scheme` taking values in
affine schemes and preserving pullbacks, and let the structure presheaf of rings on `C` be the
global regular functions of `L`, with sections raised to a chosen universe.  A presheaf of
modules on `C` which is *cartesian* — all its restriction maps are base-change isomorphisms — is
then a sheaf for any topology whose coverings refine to finite families that are flat coverings
of schemes.

Over such a covering the rings of sections form a faithfully flat family, because a finite flat
covering of an affine scheme is a faithfully flat ring map, and the double overlaps are fibre
products of affine schemes, hence pushouts of rings.  So
`Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheafFor_of_cartesian` applies, and the sheaf condition follows after
refining an arbitrary covering sieve.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Sites.liftedSchemeRings`: the presheaf of commutative rings of global regular functions
  of a functor to schemes, with sections raised to a larger universe.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.faithfullyFlat_pi_appTop`: **a finite flat covering of an affine
  scheme by affine schemes is faithfully flat on global functions.**
* `Stacks.Sites.isPushout_schemeRings_of_isPullback`: **a fibre product square of a site of
  affine schemes becomes a pushout square of the rings of global regular functions.**
* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheafFor_of_affine_flat_cover`: the sheaf axiom for one finite flat
  covering family.
* `Stacks.Sites.exists_finite_flat_refinement` and
  `Stacks.Sites.exists_finite_flat_refinement_over`: a covering sieve of a precoverage whose
  coverings are finite and flat over the schemes is refined by a single finite flat family, also
  after passing to a slice.
* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_affine_flat_covers` and
  `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_affine_flat_refinements`: **a cartesian presheaf of
  modules is a sheaf**, for a topology generated by finite flat coverings and for a topology all
  of whose coverings are refined by such.
* `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheafFor_of_cartesian_of_flat_cover`,
  `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_of_flat_covers` and
  `Stacks.PresheafOfModules.isSheaf_of_cartesian_of_flat_refinements`: the same three statements
  for an arbitrary presheaf of rings on `C`, taking as hypotheses the two facts about it that
  the proofs use — faithful flatness of the product of the restriction maps of a flat covering
  family, and that a fibre product square of the site becomes a pushout square of rings.

## Implementation notes

The structure presheaf is not fixed but passed as a presheaf `R` together with the hypothesis
`R = liftedSchemeRings L`; that is what lets a consumer whose structure sheaf arrives by another
route use these statements after a single rewriting step, rather than having to transport a
module along an isomorphism of presheaves of rings.

Flatness is used as `AlgebraicGeometry.Flat`, packaged through
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.precoverage`.  The private abbreviation `flatProperty` names that
morphism property so that the stability instances of its precoverage can be found by
`inferInstanceAs`; without the name, instance search is presented with `@Flat` eta-expanded and
does not match.

